# How we can prevent fraud best in your market in this scenario?
## Pre-authorising/Booking whenever we can the first hour/predicted payment to ensure a working payment method: _does_ _depend on user payment method as well((_{color:#bf2600}_This would be ideal.)_{color}
## Adding a Capturing logic for payments to avoid high user debt but to keep as much as we can from the pre-booked amounts: _does_ _depend on user payment method and final price difference to what we hold vs what accumulated extra_
# How can we limit fraud?
## Perhaps to limit the category only to trusted users and spenders? {color:#bf2600}_Since this is card-only, it will already apply by default. Most users are likely business clients, and we can also prompt these riders to activate pick-up codes._{color}
## Perhaps to add a final limit to the possible destinations update (trip length)? Not to allow fully endless driving through destination updates.
# How can we resolve fraud? ← This may be even the most important aspect for our discussions
## Are we covered in the local T&C to potentially protect Bolt? Under which conditions_?_ {color:#bf2600}_TBA_ {color}
## Setting up the monitoring and operational procedure to ‘save’ Bolt and action any intentional fraud scenarios
### The right to deduct ride fare due to fraud from the driver-partner
### The right to limit access to this category for those not ‘qualifying’ due to fraud suspicion{color:#bf2600} _(can be added into t&Cs)_{color} 

{color:#bf2600}_A separate search category has been created (_{color}[{color:#bf2600}_https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/system-data/categories/edit/3295_{color}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/system-data/categories/edit/3295]{color:#bf2600}_) where only card/business users can access._{color}

