{quote}Those invoices are being uploaded on behalf of BOLT SERVICES and not Bolt Operations.{quote}

The invoices for Delivery are not for provision of “Business“ services, but for the provision of Delivery Services, which is expected as per the localization model after May 5th. (Prior to that, instead of Bolt Services, the Couriers invoiced the BA). Essentially, Bolt buys the Delivery Services from Courier and Resells them. The hybrid setup for Bolt Food should be covered by T&C, but to confirm, let’s involve our colleagues from Legal team 

----

Hey [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117] TL; DR. In Romania as per the localization model from May ([link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/5924815231/Romania+Food+Localization+Billing+Scope]) the Delivery for Foo is invoiced from the Bolt entity (BOLT SERVICES RO S.R.L.) to the Customer (BA in our case) as per the hybrid Billing model. BAs claim that this contradicts the T&C, as _“they’re contracted to the Bolt Operations OU”_ and refuses to pay. Can you, please, advise or redirect, what should be communicated to the Customers.

----

{quote}Can we at least have a single invoice for all the food delivery orders included and sent once in efactura?{quote}

Unfortunately, the Resale Billing Model (one invoice) currently is not supported for the Food operations. Development would require involvement from Product, Tax and Engineering team.

{quote}But when they also receive 1000 other small delivery fees, it is like forcing them to pay it twice.{quote}

The BA is invoiced only once with the Delivery Invoice, which is then being sent to SPV. I believe the confusion stems from the Statement, which is issued at the EOM. Worth noting that Statement is not valid for the VAT accounting, and shouldn’t be used as such.

Based on the discussion with Tax: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07AAVC09D4/p1749813356839239?thread_ts=1749643289.316159&cid=C07AAVC09D4|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07AAVC09D4/p1749813356839239?thread_ts=1749643289.316159&cid=C07AAVC09D4], it’s not possible to just stop issuing such invoices.

I think the problem lies entirely in the auth. There is a chance that OAuth credentials are overriding access when trying to validate databricks bundle files. Can you please try removing this file:

{noformat}rm -f ~/.databricks/token-cache.json{noformat}

In fact, I suggest removing this databricks completely, {{rm -f ~/.databrickscfg}}, and recreating only using the {{databricks configure}} command. Also, try using the same token as the dbt token in profiles.

